# ── npm-internal package CVEs (resolved) ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# Trivy previously reported HIGH/MEDIUM findings for npm-internal packages
# (ip-address, brace-expansion, tar, undici) bundled inside the Node base image.
# npm is never executed at runtime — the app runs purely as a `node` process.
#
# Resolution: npm is removed from the production runner stage in the Dockerfile,
# and the Node base image is pinned to 22.23.2 (undici 6.28.0 in Node itself).
#
# If new npm-internal CVEs appear after a base-image bump, either:
#   1. Remove npm from the runner stage again (preferred), or
#   2. Add the CVE ID here with a comment explaining zero runtime attack surface.
